---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { creatorsFor, games, publicEntries } from '../lib/content/load';
// Who our guide facts come from, counted from the published entries' own source lists.
const counts = new Map<string, number>();
let total = 0;
for (const g of games) for (const e of publicEntries(g.id)) {
  total++;
  for (const p of new Set(e.sources.map((s) => s.publisher))) counts.set(p, (counts.get(p) ?? 0) + 1);
}
const publishers = [...counts].sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1] || a[0].localeCompare(b[0]));
const creators = games.flatMap((g) => creatorsFor(g.id));
---
<Prose title="Credits" description="Where our guide information comes from, what we use and under what terms.">
  <p>We'd rather be clear than vague about this. Here's what the guides are built from, and how each thing is used.</p>

  <h2>Guide text</h2>
  <p>Every guide entry is written by us in our own words. We don't copy other guides' text. Each entry lists the pages its facts came from
  and the date we checked them, under "Sources and last checked". Across our {total} published entries, these are cited:</p>
  <ul class="pubs">
    {publishers.map(([p, n]) => <li><strong>{p}</strong> <span class="muted">· {n} {n === 1 ? 'entry' : 'entries'}</span></li>)}
  </ul>
  <p class="muted small">Citing a source means we used it to check facts, not that the source endorses us or has given permission beyond what's listed below.</p>

  <h2>Creator videos</h2>
  <p>Videos stay on YouTube and play in YouTube's own player, only after you press play. All rights belong to the creators.
  {creators.length > 0 && <>Creators whose public uploads we follow: {creators.map((c, i) => <>{i > 0 && ', '}<a href={`https://www.youtube.com/channel/${c.channelId}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{c.name}</a></>)}.</>}
  Our daily check uses the YouTube API Services (see <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>).</p>

  <h2>Map</h2>
  <p>Map locations and the coastline and road outlines come from <a href="https://github.com/fbritoferreira/gta6" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open GTA 6 Map</a>
  by fbritoferreira and contributors, under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY 4.0</a>.
  We filtered the records, simplified the outlines and drew our own map and pins. No game map tiles, screenshots or art are used.</p>

  <h2>Images and design</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The game card art on the Games page is our own drawing. We don't use publisher logos, key art or screenshots.</li>
    <li>The Nerdy Birdie logo and the "Brick by Brick" banner belong to NerdyBirdie LLC. COZMC's wordmark and mascots are used with COZMC's permission.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Software and fonts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Fonts: Inter, Space Grotesk, Pixelify Sans and Press Start 2P, under the SIL Open Font License, served from this site.</li>
    <li>Built with Astro, Preact and Zod (MIT License). Map display by Leaflet (BSD 2-Clause License).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Trademarks</h2>
  <p>NerdyBirdie LLC Gaming Guides is independent and unofficial. It is not affiliated with, endorsed or sponsored by Rockstar Games, Take-Two Interactive,
  Microsoft/Xbox or Sony Interactive Entertainment/PlayStation. Grand Theft Auto and all related names are trademarks of their owners and are used
  here only to say which game a guide is about.</p>

  <h2>Something wrong?</h2>
  <p>If you own something here and think it's used wrongly or without credit, or a source is missing, <a href="/corrections/#report">report it</a>.</p>
</Prose>
<style>
  .pubs { columns: 2 220px; }
</style>
